=== 22:22 PRE-REGISTRATION (H2H) -- head-to-head on the tasks built to discriminate: zakcode (35B and 27B, local) vs Claude Code (as ships)
Written before any run. Why: the campaign goal is parity with Claude Code as an agent; ADR-0156 measured 3/3 vs 3/3 on 06/07/08
(N=1) and no head-to-head has ever been run on the Mind-turn tasks m01-m05, which test agent BEHAVIOUR (checking a negative claim,
not reading a 0 as a measurement, minimal diffs, asserting not hedging, reading before editing) rather than code-writing.
Tasks (6): m01-stale-doc-negative, m02-ambiguous-zero, m03-minimal-diff, m04-assert-not-hedge, m05-read-before-edit,
06-plugin-conventions. Every workspace ships WITHOUT any .claude/rules -- both agents run as they ship, no rule text injected.
Arms:
  CC       Claude Code 2.1.267 on this box, model claude-fable-5-1 (the operator default; probe: 1 turn, $0.148), the arm's
           canonical invocation (claude -p <prompt> --allowedTools Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Glob,Grep --output-format json), N=2
           per task (Claude Code exposes no temperature; the repeat measures its own consistency). Expected cost ~$3-4.
  ZAK-35B  zakcode on zds-qwen3.6-35b, zc-01, temp 0, ZAKCODE_STABLE_PROMPT_IDENTITY=1, ZBENCH_PIN_MODE=workspace, bench default
           (no catalogue, no rules), N=3 per task.
  ZAK-27B  same on zds-qwen3.8-27b, N=3 per task. The 27B is the small-model target; the 35B is the coach's classify engine.
Per-task verdicts (the task is the replication unit -- rb-10837; no pooled parity score is claimed):
  PARITY   CC passes >= 1/2 and zakcode passes >= 2/3.
  GAP      CC passes >= 1/2 and zakcode passes <= 1/3 -- named, with the verify reason, as the next fix cycle's input.
  CEILING  CC passes 0/2 -- the task is beyond the reference too; zakcode's result on it is reported, not judged.
  EDGE     CC passes 0/2 and zakcode passes >= 2/3 -- reported as such; one task never establishes superiority.
Predictions: P1 CC passes all six (>= 1/2 each). P2 ZAK-35B: m02 FAILS 0/3 (m02-arms.log: 0/6 on the quick_code arm), 06 passes
(ADR-0156), m01/m03/m05 pass (ADR-0147's stable instrument), m04 not predicted. P3 ZAK-27B passes no more tasks than ZAK-35B and
passes 06 3/3 (tonight's CAT NONE cell). P4 the expected GAP list is {m02} for the 35B and {m02, possibly m04} for the 27B.
Instrument refusals (not results): a run without a report (no_report), a verify that cannot run, a CC run with is_error.
Reported beside the verdicts: seconds per run, CC dollars per run, turns/iterations. Results appended below, box-clock stamped.

